[Applause]  it's only three days into his presidency  and pedro castillo is already facing  protests angry  at his choice of prime minister  [Applause]  criminal terrorists want to rule the  country it's not fair that a terrorist  as prime minister  that's why we're protesting  we will not allow terrorists to take  over our country  is being investigated for an alleged  apology for terrorism  which is a crime in peru in an interview  earlier this year  he defended members of the shining path  the maoist rebel group that killed  tens of thousands of people from the  1980s onwards  castillo's choice of vegido for prime  minister or cabinet chief  as it's known in peru sent shockwaves  around the country  the stock market dropped along with the  value of peru's currency against the  dollar  critics also say other new ministers  have no  experience in government  we can't say it's a lack of intelligence  experience or that he's never governed  and that's why he's making all these  mistakes no  i think there is much more to it because  the president signaled his divisiveness  and all peruvians will bear the brunt of  his irresponsibility  well many people here say they didn't  vote for castillo but many who did are  expressing their anger through social  media  saying they voted for him to rule for  the people and not  for the political party he represents so  far  president castillo has also visited  victims of an earthquake  in the north of the country telling  supporters he'll focus on those left  behind  there are people who have been left  behind for a very long time  we can't do much if we don't prioritize  our health care we will give mayors and  regional governors  a better budget  many peruvians want castillo to deliver  the changes he promised  during his election campaign but it'll  be hard for them  to trust the president who they say has  been making mistakes  from day one mariana sanchez al jazeera  lima peru

